Scale by adding an constant offset to your linear predictor. To follow Andrews example of scaling by a million: add ln(1e6) to eta as you feed it into neg_binomial_2_log. For problems with large numbers, this should improve computational efficiency. I don't think it will help prevent the sum of ln(1e6) and eta from reaching 1e9, but at least the values of the model parameters underlying linear predictor eta won't be so ridiculously large.

