Message-ID: <_sDzHTM8iOg.W0rqJ7CO1n8J@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <_sDzHTM8iOg.-NJvx-Y7RUwJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <_sDzHTM8iOg.-NJvx-Y7RUwJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/_sDzHTM8iOg/m/W0rqJ7CO1n8J>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

monitor() by default throws away the first half of whatever array you give it, and as.array() throws away the warmup. So, monitor(as.array(stanfit)) throws away half the post-burnin. Call it with warmup = 0.

Ben

