In addition to what you listed, lp__ also includes Jacobian adjustments for bounded parameters (which are sampled on the unconstrained scale, remember). So whatever you calculate "manually" will be different from lp__ (even if you take account of the constants that are dropped), unless there are no constrained parameters in your model (which is not the case for you, as the "sigma"-parameters are constrained to be positive).

