On Tuesday, May 26, 2015 at 11:25:03 PM UTC-4, Cindy Lim wrote:
> Lambda is calculated based on the parameters K,Q and b, which will cause it to be a real rather than an integer. This is then passed on to the Poisson distribution in the model block. I was wondering if there is any way to get around the integer declaration, please?

No. The Poisson distribution is for integer counts and in Stan, such counts must be declared as data.

