Krzysztof,

Thanks for the reply. Unpacking z makes a lot of sense, thank you for pointing that out. I just want to make sure I've got this right, as I had to make an assumption regarding how to actually include my observed data.

Here is a brief model block. The full stan file is attached.

T is total number of time windows (31 fyi), N is total number of individuals (~2000), sight is the NxT matrix of presence/absence, p is sampling, phi is survival, and gamma is birth:

model {
  real running;
  vector[T] total;

  running <- 0;

  for(n in 1:N) {
    for(t in T:1) {
      running <- log(phi[t]) + log(1 - p[t]) + running;
      total[t] <- running + log(gamma[t]);
      increment_log_prob(bernoulli_log(sight[n, t],
        log_sum_exp(log(p[t]), running)));
    }
  }
}

Does this look appropriate? I'm pretty sure I messed up the increment statement, though the attached stan file does compile.

I really appreciate this, thank you.

Cheers,

Peter

