Dear all,

Thanks so much for your comments! Have realised where I went wrong in the code. Declared I wrongly in the parameter block when it should be in the data block, and have also declared it as an integer type. Have also converted the priors to stan code accordingly.

For missing data, the reference manual suggested coding the observed data and missing data separately, where N_obs is the number of observed data and N_mis is the number of missing data. In this model, the number of missing values differ for D,V,Z and W and are dependent on time. Not sure if I understand the section clearly, but to include missing values, I should be amending the model code chunk to something like the following?

model {

for (j in 1:nobs)
{
I[j] ~ poisson(pop*lambda[j]);

delta_D[j] ~ binomial(I[j],pD);

delta_V[j] ~ binomial(I[j],pV);

delta_Z[j] ~ binomial(I[j],pZ);

delta_W[j] ~ poisson(thetaW*pW*I[j]);
}

for (k in 1:D_mis)
  {
delta_Dmis[k] ~ binomial(I[j],pD);
}

for (k in 1:V_mis)
  {
delta_Vmis[k] ~ binomial(I[j],pV);
}

for (k in 1:Z_mis)
  {
delta_Zmis[k] ~ binomial(I[j],pZ);
}

for (k in 1:W_mis)
  {
delta_Wmis[k] ~ poisson(thetaW*pW*I[j]);
}

}

where D_mis, V_mis, W_mis and Z_mis are the number of missing values in delta_D, delta_V, delta_W and delta_Z, respectively. I will then replace the NAs in the dataset with the parameters delta_Dmis, delta_Vmis, delta_Wmis and delta_Zmis for delta_D, delta_V, delta_W and delta_Z.

Is my understanding correct, please?

Many thanks!

Regards,
Cindy

